IMPORT prelude

-- Vandalism Act 1966 (Singapore) -- what an "act of vandalism" is (s 2), the offence and its punishment, including when
-- caning must be imposed (s 3), producing written authority or consent on demand (s 4), seizure (s 5), arrestable and
-- non-bailable (s 6), the presumption on receiving stolen public property (s 7), and revocation of a secondhand goods
-- dealer's licence (s 8).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/VA1966.txt. The
-- deposit says it "incorporates all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021 and comes into operation on
-- 31 December 2021". No later amendment is annotated in the deposit.
--
-- The arrangement of sections at the top of the deposit is out of step with the body (it numbers "Short title" as 2);
-- the BODY's numbers are followed here: s 1 short title, s 2 interpretation, s 3 penalty, s 4 production on demand,
-- s 5 seizure, s 6 arrestable, s 7 presumption, s 8 revocation of licence.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Cited by 6 of the 527 Singapore Acts deposited in this repository. The whole Act is eight short sections;
-- every operative section is encoded. Not encoded: the effect of ss 325(1) and 330(1) of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010,
-- to which caning is "subject" (taken here as a single input flag -- what those sections say was not read); what
-- "arrestable" and "non-bailable" entail under that Code; the content of s 411 of the Penal Code 1871; sentencing within
-- the maxima.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Vandalism Act 1966`

§§ `2 -- act of vandalism`

-- s 2 "act of vandalism" means --
-- (a) without the written authority of an authorised officer or representative of the Government [etc.] "in the case of
--     public property, or without the written consent of the owner or occupier in the case of private property" --
--     (i) "writing, drawing, painting, marking or inscribing" on any public or private property any word, slogan,
--         caricature, drawing, mark, symbol or other thing;
--     (ii) "affixing, posting up or displaying" any poster, placard, advertisement, bill, notice, paper or other document;
--     (iii) "hanging, suspending, hoisting, affixing or displaying" any flag, bunting, standard, banner or the like with
--         any word, slogan [etc.]; or
-- (b) "stealing, destroying or damaging any public property".
-- "public property": property "belonging to the Government or to the government of any Commonwealth or foreign country
-- or to any statutory body or authority or to any armed force lawfully present in Singapore". "private property":
-- property "other than public property".
--
-- Paragraph (b) carries no "without written authority" qualifier, and reaches only PUBLIC property. Damaging private
-- property is not an act of vandalism under this Act at all (it may be an offence elsewhere -- not read).
DECLARE Conduct IS ONE OF
    `writing or marking on property`
    `posting up a poster or notice`
    `hanging a flag or banner with a slogan`
    `stealing property`
    `destroying property`
    `damaging property`

DECLARE Owner IS ONE OF
    `the Government`
    `a foreign government`
    `a statutory body`
    `an armed force lawfully present in Singapore`
    `a private company`
    `a private individual`

GIVEN `the owner` IS AN Owner
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the property is public property` IF
    CONSIDER `the owner`
    WHEN `a private company` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a private individual` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the conduct` IS A Conduct
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is paragraph (a) conduct` IF
    CONSIDER `the conduct`
    WHEN `writing or marking on property` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `posting up a poster or notice` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `hanging a flag or banner with a slogan` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- `had written permission` stands for the written authority (public property) or the written consent of the owner or
-- occupier (private property), whichever paragraph (a) requires for the property concerned.
GIVEN `the conduct` IS A Conduct, `the owner` IS AN Owner, `had written permission` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is an act of vandalism` IF
        (`is paragraph (a) conduct` `the conduct` AND (NOT `had written permission`))
    OR  ((NOT `is paragraph (a) conduct` `the conduct`) AND `the property is public property` `the owner`)

§§ `3 -- penalty for acts of vandalism`

-- s 3: "any person who commits any act of vandalism or attempts to do any such act or causes any such act to be done shall
-- be guilty of an offence" -- "a fine not exceeding $2,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 3 years, and shall
-- also, subject to sections 325(1) and 330(1) of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010, be punished with caning with not less
-- than 3 strokes and not more than 8 strokes".
GIVEN `committed it` IS A BOOLEAN, `attempted it` IS A BOOLEAN, `caused it to be done` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a section 3 offence` IF
    `committed it` OR `attempted it` OR `caused it to be done`

GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `maximum fine in dollars` IS 2000

GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `maximum imprisonment in months` IS 36

GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `minimum strokes of the cane` IS 3

GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `maximum strokes of the cane` IS 8

-- s 3, proviso: caning "shall not be imposed on a first conviction under this Act in the case of any act falling within --
-- (a) paragraph (a)(i) ... if the writing, drawing, mark or inscription is done with pencil, crayon, chalk or other delible
-- substance or thing and not with paint, tar or other indelible substance or thing; or (b) paragraph (a)(ii) or (iii)".
--
-- So caning is mandatory on a first conviction for marking in paint, and for any stealing, destroying or damaging of
-- public property; posters and flags escape caning only on a FIRST conviction.
GIVEN `the conduct` IS A Conduct, `first conviction under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN, `done with a delible substance` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the first-conviction exception applies` IF
    `first conviction under this Act` AND
        CONSIDER `the conduct`
        WHEN `writing or marking on property` THEN `done with a delible substance`
        WHEN `posting up a poster or notice` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `hanging a flag or banner with a slogan` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE

-- `excluded by CPC ss 325(1) or 330(1)` is an input: the Act makes caning "subject to" those sections, which were not read.
GIVEN `the conduct` IS A Conduct, `first conviction under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN, `done with a delible substance` IS A BOOLEAN, `excluded by CPC ss 325(1) or 330(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `caning must be imposed` IF
        (NOT `the first-conviction exception applies` `the conduct` `first conviction under this Act` `done with a delible substance`)
    AND (NOT `excluded by CPC ss 325(1) or 330(1)`)

§§ `4 and 5 -- production on demand and seizure`

-- s 4(1): the written authority or consent "shall be produced on demand to any member of the Singapore Police Force or of
-- the Special Constabulary or of the Auxiliary Police Force or to any member of the naval, military or air force police
-- attached to the Singapore Armed Forces or to any armed force lawfully present in Singapore".
-- (2): "Any person who fails, refuses or neglects to produce such written authority or written consent on demand" --
-- "a fine not exceeding $500".
-- s 5: "Any person mentioned in section 4(1) may seize any poster, placard, bunting, paper or document or any other
-- article or thing in respect of which he reasonably believes an offence to have been committed under this Act or which
-- he reasonably believes to be or to contain evidence relating to such an offence."
DECLARE Demander IS ONE OF
    `a Singapore Police Force officer`
    `a Special Constabulary member`
    `an Auxiliary Police Force officer`
    `SAF military police`
    `police of a foreign armed force lawfully present`
    `a private security guard`
    `a town council officer`
    `the property owner`

GIVEN `the demander` IS A Demander
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a section 4(1) person` IF
    CONSIDER `the demander`
    WHEN `a private security guard` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a town council officer` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `the property owner` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the demander` IS A Demander, `produced it on demand` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `failing to produce is an offence` IF
    `is a section 4(1) person` `the demander` AND (NOT `produced it on demand`)

GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `maximum fine for failing to produce in dollars` IS 500

GIVEN `the demander` IS A Demander, `reasonably believes it relates to an offence or is evidence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may seize the article` IF
    `is a section 4(1) person` `the demander` AND `reasonably believes it relates to an offence or is evidence`

§§ `6 -- arrestable and non-bailable`

-- s 6: "Every offence under the provisions of this Act shall be arrestable and non-bailable for the purposes of the
-- Criminal Procedure Code 2010." This includes the $500 s 4(2) offence.
DECLARE Offence IS ONE OF
    `the section 3 vandalism offence`
    `the section 4(2) failure to produce offence`
    `receiving stolen public property under Penal Code s 411`

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is arrestable and non-bailable under this Act` IF
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `receiving stolen public property under Penal Code s 411` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `7 and 8 -- stolen public property`

-- s 7: in a prosecution under s 411 of the Penal Code 1871, "where the stolen property is public property, it shall be
-- presumed, until the contrary is proved, that the person who received or retained that property knew or had reason to
-- believe that the property was stolen public property and also that such person received or retained it dishonestly".
GIVEN `prosecuted under Penal Code s 411` IS A BOOLEAN, `the owner` IS AN Owner
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the knowledge and dishonesty presumption applies` IF
    `prosecuted under Penal Code s 411` AND `the property is public property` `the owner`

-- s 8: where a secondhand goods dealer "is convicted under section 411 of the Penal Code 1871 and the stolen property
-- concerned is public property, the court SHALL, in addition to any other penalty that it may impose, revoke any licence or
-- exemption granted under that Act".
GIVEN `is a secondhand goods dealer` IS A BOOLEAN, `convicted under Penal Code s 411` IS A BOOLEAN, `the owner` IS AN Owner
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the court must revoke the dealer's licence` IF
    `is a secondhand goods dealer` AND `convicted under Penal Code s 411` AND `the property is public property` `the owner`
